  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Aircraft Manufacturing (NAICS 336411) has attracted $35.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, accounting for $34.6B of those obligations. Obligations are down 42.5% year over year. Contracting activity includes 4,537 awards and an average award size of $7.8M. Historical fiscal year totals show material variation, with FY21 at $40.7B, FY22 at $37.2B, FY23 at $60.1B, FY24 at $44.2B, and FY25 at $61.2B. Prime vendors concentrate a large share of obligations: LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION led with $9.3B, followed by multiple entries for THE BOEING COMPANY totaling several high-value awards including $5.8B, $3.3B, $2.4B, $1.6B, and $1.2B. Sikorsky and Bell Textron also appear among top vendors with $2.5B and $1.8B respectively. Non-DoD civil buyers show much smaller programs, led by the Department of Homeland Security at $136M and the Department of Commerce at $108M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
